SUMMARY:Lake Berryessa - Oak Shores
DESCRIPTION:Kayaking Sonoma County & Beyond\n**Description**\nPaddle at La
 ke Berryessa - Oak Shores Day use area. This is a great place for paddlers
  of all levels. The main area that we will be paddling is a designated no 
 wake zone\, this means no speeding power boats and big wakes to deal with.
  There is a long semi paved foot path to the lake from the parking lot whi
 ch leads to a nice beach for launching.\nPLEASE BRING YOUR KAYAK CARTS.\n\
 nWhile we are on the water we will have time to practice skills and get ti
 ps and tricks on how to become more efficient at those skills. We could al
 so see some great wildlife so bring binoculars and a camera / phone for pi
 ctures.\nWe will meet on the shore at Oak Shores Day Use Area around the a
 rea where the foot path connects to the beach.\n\n**Boat Length Requiremen
 ts / Recommendations**\nAll Kayaks (including inflatables) and Canoes and 
 SUPs are welcome\n\n**Paddle Level**\nAll Skill Levels are welcome - This 
 event will be great for beginners and novice paddlers\n\n**Schedule:**\n9:
 00 am - Meet on the beach\n9:30 am - Pre Paddle meeting and OTW\nIf you ne
 ed more time to set up your boat then please arrive earlier.\nWe will be o
 n the water (OTW) on time.\n4:00 pm - approximate return time to the beach
  where we started at.\n\n**What to Bring**\nKayak\, Paddle\n***PFD (must b
 e worn while we are on the water)***\nVHF radio if you have one.\nWater\, 
 Lunch\, Snacks\nKayak cart\nBinoculars and Camera - to view the wildlife.\
 nDry change of clothes in a dry bag in your boat.\nDry change of clothes i
 n your car for after the paddle.\n\nReminder: You can never have to many l
 ayers to put on when you get cold.\n\n**Parking / Launch Fees**\n$5 for th
 e Oak Shores Day Use area\n\n**IMPORTANT PLEASE READ**\nIn RSVP'ing for th
 is event you are declaring that the organizer\, event hosts\, and leaders 
 of this group are not responsible and/or liable for anything that happens 
 to you or your gear. YOU are responsible and Liable for your own safety an
 d the safety of your gear. If you are bringing a guest then you are taking
  full responsibility and liability for them and their gear and anything th
 at they do.\nThe organizers of this trip are not experts\, not professiona
 l tour guides and do not necessarily have safety training or carry any saf
 ety equipment. Each paddler must have the training\, experience and equipm
 ent required to complete this paddle safely\, and must assume all personal
  risks and liabilities.
URL;VALUE=URI:https://www.meetup.com/kayaking-sonoma-beyond/events/3157045
 41/
